# Reproduction

    python3 analysis/summed_social_capital.py     # full log -> stdout (saved to output/full_log.txt)

Reads only `data/capital.csv`, `data/time_series_data.csv`, `data/pollen_openness_score_Belau_Woserin_Feeser_et_al_2019.csv`.
`capital.csv` must be read with `decimal=','`. Raw pollen columns (`pollen`, `Belau_PC1`, `Woserin_PC1`, ~95% NaN) are never used; only
`_inter` / `MEAN` / `SMOOTH_MEAN_*`. `calBP = 1950 - CE_signed`.

Sections: A raw SC series · B peak stability across 50/100/150/200/250-yr smoothing for SC (3 index variants) and the other three blocks
· C per-component diagnostics at both tied peak bins (pre-registered rule) · D block-level comparison · E tie-aware concordance with
`time_series_data.csv` (raw anchors + annual `_inter` grid) · F secondary pollen check (reported, not used as mechanism) · G ASCII panels + `output/summary.json`.

Outputs: `output/component_table.csv`, `output/stability_table.csv`, `output/block_table.csv`, `output/summary.json`, `output/hypothesis.md`.
Matplotlib is unavailable in this environment, so section G prints ASCII panels instead of a PNG.
